# The shell scripts run on Linux in CI and in Git Bash on Windows, and a CRLF line
# ending breaks both: `set -euo pipefail\r` is not a valid option name. With
# core.autocrlf=true every checkout would hand Windows a CRLF copy, so the checkout is
# pinned to LF here regardless of that setting. The index already holds these files
# with LF, so this changes nothing about what is committed — only what a checkout
# writes back out.
*.sh text eol=lf
